      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MOSTERT NZ (10) is a newcomer to the Chantal Turpin yard from NZ and brings consistent form having recorded a win and three placings from his last four attempts at Addington. Hasn't raced for seven weeks and cops a back row draw but won his lone attempt at this distance. GREASED LIGHTNIN NZ (7) was racing well before a six-week let-up, placing in his last two outings here. Draws much wider this time but has been kept up to the mark with an easy trial win. FIFTY THREE STARS (2) came from this barrier and dug deep to get home last start, taking his record at this circuit and distance to four from five. Could strike again. GREATGREAT BOULDER (4) will be reaching peak fitness now and could be close to a win after placing in his last two appearances here, the latest from the back row. GREAT ACHIEVER (1) draws to be competitive.",
